    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5126" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellĭger</span></b> , ĕra,
			ĕrum, adj.
		bellum-gero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>waging war</i>, <i>warlike</i>, <i>martial</i>, <i>valiant</i> (<b>poet.</b>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">esp. freq. in the post-Aug. per.): gentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 3, 11, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 124</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Augustus, Claud. in Prob. et Olybr Cons. 74:
					Hannibal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. 1,
					38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">numen,</span>”
				i.e. <i>Mars</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. Achill. 1, 504</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fera,</span>”
				i.e. <i>the elephant used in war</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					8, 261</span></i>
			.—</div>
